      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Rheumatoid disease is a systemic disorder affecting multiple organs. It is known to affect the nervous system in a variety of ways, but its presentation with spinal cord compression by a rheumatoid nodule is rare. We report two cases presenting with cord compression by a rheumatoid nodule who underwent surgical decompression with good recovery."},
